# Configuration

#### General Environment Variables
<hr class="section-rule lvl-4">

The knobs you're most likely to set.  All are ordinary environment variables (or `?=`
overrides); the defaults shown are what ships.

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `CMK_DIND` | `0` | Opt into docker-in-docker for container-dispatch (`1` = dispatch runs a nested daemon). |
| `CMK_PRE` | `flux.noop` | Space-separated targets run **before** the main pipeline, during the bootloader stage; a failing pre-target aborts. |
| `CMK_POST` | `flux.noop` | Space-separated targets run **at exit**, on success or failure. |
| `CMK_SUPERVISOR` | `1` | Run under the supervisor/trampoline; `0` disables it (e.g. a nested subcommand dispatch). |
| `CMK_MODULES_DIR` | `.cmk` | Directory searched for importable modules; its first element also seeds the staging dir. |
| `CMK_PLUGINS_DIR` | `.cmk` | Directory searched for plugin `.cmk` blocks. |
| `CMK_XDG_CACHE` | `~/.cache/compose.mk` | Cache root (honors `XDG_CACHE_HOME`); the `CMK_STAGE_DIR` fallback for read-only / global installs. |
| `CMK_COMPILER_VERBOSE` | `1` | Compiler-logging chatter; a direct `cmk run` forces `0`. |
| `CMK_LOG_IMPORTS` | `0` | Log routine import chatter (errors always print). |
| `verbose` | `1` | Show `compose.mk` internal logging (`0` = quieter). |
| `quiet` | `0` | Suppress docker build output (`1` = quiet builds). |
| `force` | `0` | Force otherwise-skipped operations (docker pulls, etc). |
| `trace` / `TRACE` | `0` | Very noisy: append `-x` to most shell invocations. |

`CMK_STANDALONE`, `CMK_LIB`, `CMK_INTERNAL`, and `CMK_IN_CONTAINER` are **read-only** state
flags the runtime sets to reflect the execution context (stand-alone vs. library, and whether
you're inside a recursive sub-make or a dispatch container); read them, don't set them.
`CMK_SRC` / `CMK_BIN` are covered by the self-path family below, and `CMK_STAGE_DIR` by the
scratch-vs-staging section.

#### TUI Environment Variables
<hr class="section-rule lvl-4">

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `TUI_THEME_NAME` | `powerline/double/green` | tmux/powerline theme for the embedded TUI. |
| `TUI_CONTAINER_IMAGE` | `compose.mk:tux` | Image backing the TUI container. |
| `TUI_SVC_NAME` | `tux` | Compose service name for the TUI container. |
| `TUI_TMUX_SESSION_NAME` | `tui` | tmux session name the TUI runs in. |
| `TUI_BOOTSTRAP` | `tux.require` | Target that bootstraps the TUI stack before launch. |

The remaining `TUI_*` names (init callbacks, theme hooks, tmux socket, service build order,
compose file) are internal wiring the framework sets for you; override them only if you're
customizing the TUI's plumbing.

