#### "Where does compose.mk write?" (scratch vs. staging)
<hr class="section-rule lvl-4">

Runtime files fall into two categories, so there is deliberately **no** `CMK_TMP_DIR`:

* **Container-visible scratch** lives under the working directory (the `.tmp.*` /
  `io.mktemp` convention, with `TMPDIR` pinned to the current directory).  Container-dispatch bind-mounts
  the cwd to `/workspace`, so a launched container reads this scratch by the same
  relative path; a system-`/tmp` temp would be invisible to it.
* **Host-only cache and staging** (the materialized `.tmp.module.*`, the native-compile
  cache, the remade `__hosted__` cache) lives under `CMK_STAGE_DIR`.  It resolves to
  `CMK_MODULES_DIR` when that dir is writable (the vendored `./.cmk`, still under the
  workspace mount), to an explicitly-set staging dir when you point one there, and
  otherwise to `CMK_XDG_CACHE` (`~/.cache/compose.mk`).  That last fallback is what lets
  a global / `pip` install keep working when its default `CMK_MODULES_DIR` is the
  read-only bundled plugins share, and keeps `compose.mk <target>` in an arbitrary
  directory from creating a stray `./.cmk`.

{{ macros.section(4, "Dunder Names", id="dunder-names") }}

`compose.mk` reserves a handful of **double-underscore names** for special roles.  Most are
ordinary (exported) make-variables that exist at parse/run-time; two are exported *registries*;
and a couple are [cmk-lang]({{_}}/cmk/compiler) **dialect placeholders** that
only exist at compile-time (the compiler rewrites them before `make` ever sees them).  Each is
documented in depth on the linked page; this list is just the index.

<div class="def-cards">
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__main__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">entrypoint</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>The default goal (<code>.DEFAULT_GOAL</code>), run when no target is named; every CMK file declares a <code>__main__:</code> rule (the compiler injects a stub if one is missing).</p><p>Pythonic: it runs on <em>direct</em> execution, but on <em>import</em> a module/plugin's <code>__main__</code> is demoted to a plain <code>&lt;name&gt;:</code> target, so it never collides with the importer's own.</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/cmk/modules#executable-modules">Executable Modules</a>, <a href="{{_}}/runtime">Runtime</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__doc__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">docstring</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>The module's own docstring: a bare column-0 triple-quote (<code>'''&hellip;'''</code>) at the top of a CMK file lowers to <code>define __doc__ &hellip; endef</code>, interpolable as <code>${__doc__}</code>.  Pythonic.</p><p>A namespaced <code>${__name__}.__doc__</code> copy is emitted too, awaiting <code>__name__</code> tracking.</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming">Metaprogramming</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__file__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">self-path</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>The active file: <code>CMK_SRC</code> in stand-alone mode, the invoked file in library mode.</p><p class="def-card-see">the self-path table above</p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__cmk__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">self-path</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>This program, as an invokable: the <code>argv0</code> of the current boot.  Inside an interpreted run that is the compiled artifact, so <code>$__cmk__ target</code> re-enters the same program while skipping the compile front door.  It rides the standard docker env crossing workspace-relative, so a block can re-invoke its own program from inside a container, and through dind.</p><p class="def-card-see">the self-path table above</p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__interpreter__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">self-path</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>The hosting <code>compose.mk</code>, in exec form: set once at the first boot and inherited by re-invocations.  The docker crossing rewrites it to the path valid where the block stands (the workspace copy, or the mounted <code>/usr/local/bin/compose.mk</code>).  Contrast <code>__cmk__</code> (this program) and <code>CMK_BIN</code> (the raw invocation path of the current boot).</p><p class="def-card-see">the self-path table above</p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__interpreting__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">self-path</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p><code>CMK_SRC</code> unless overridden; occasionally useful to extensions.</p><p class="def-card-see">the self-path table above</p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__plugins__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">registry</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>Exported registry of loaded plugin tokens, backing <code>__plugins__.has</code> / <code>.require</code> / <code>.assert</code> (and the recipe-level <code>assert.plugin</code>).</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/plugins/overview">Plugins</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__modules__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">registry</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>Exported registry of imported module names, backing <code>__modules__.has</code> / <code>.require</code> / <code>.assert</code>.</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/cmk/modules">Modules</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__target_name__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">dialect</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>Callform-safe placeholder for <code>${@}</code>: the current target's name.</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming">Dialects</a>, <a href="{{_}}/cmk/quickref">Quick Ref</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__target__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">dialect</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>Recursive self-call to the current target; lowers to <code>this.__target_name__</code>.  Call-forms:</p><ul><li><code>__target__</code>: bare (re-run the target)</li><li><code>__target__(args)</code>: with call args</li><li><code>__target__[stream]</code>: with a piped stream</li></ul><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming">Dialects</a>, <a href="{{_}}/cmk/quickref">Quick Ref</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__target__.__doc__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">dialect</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>The running target's docstring, resolved lazily at runtime from its <code>@#</code> recipe comments (a <code>'''&hellip;'''</code> first recipe line lowers to <code>@#</code>).</p><p>Reuses the CLI-help extractor, so it costs nothing unless a recipe references it.</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming">Dialects</a>, <a href="{{_}}/cmk/quickref">Quick Ref</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__call__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">callable</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>The canonical invoke dunder: a bare <code>NAME()</code> routes here when the name defines <code>.__call__</code>, else falls back to the base call (<code>$(call NAME)</code> / <code>${make} NAME</code>).  Every <code>dsl</code> instance is stamped a default; an author overrides it (e.g. to dispatch the block into a container ambient).  Backs the <code>callable</code> protocol.</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/cmk/banana">Banana Forms</a>, <a href="{{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming">Metaprogramming</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__args__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">callable</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>Inside a callable's <code>.__call__</code> / constructor-instance body, the positional args the call received (<code>$(1)</code>); guarded undefined-safe for <code>--warn-undefined-variables</code>.</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/cmk/banana">Banana Forms</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__vm__</code></span><span class="def-card-kind">reflection</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>Reflects the running VM / control callstack.</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/modules/virtual-machine">CMK Virtual Machine</a></p></div>
  </details>
  <details class="def-card" open>
    <summary class="def-card-head"><span class="def-card-name"><code>__ip__</code> / <code>__step__</code> / …</span><span class="def-card-kind">reflection</span></summary>
    <div class="def-card-body"><p>The scheduler's seven registers: <code>__ip__</code> (C, the instruction pointer), <code>__step__</code>/<code>__step_budget__</code>, <code>__alt__</code>/<code>__yielded__</code>, and <code>__posix_code__</code> vs <code>__exit_code__</code> (raw wait status vs resolved code), exported on every dispatch hop as a read-only reflection surface, defaulted empty so an unsupervised read is safe.  The cheap always-on layer the <code>__vm__</code> snapshot reads from.</p><p class="def-card-see"><a href="{{_}}/runtime#flat-dispatch">Runtime</a></p></div>
  </details>
</div>

!!! tip "Parse-time vs. compile-time"
    `__target_name__` and `__target__` are **dialect substitutions**: they are rewritten by the
    [compiler]({{_}}/cmk/compiler) at lowering time and never reach `make`.
    Everything else is an ordinary exported make-variable available at parse/run-time, so it also
    flows into recursive `make` calls and dispatched containers.

#### About `.PHONY`
<hr class="section-rule lvl-4">

`make` treats a target as already built when a file or directory of the same name exists, which
would let a project file (say a `help` script or an `io/` subdirectory) silently shadow the matching
`compose.mk` target into a no-op.  To prevent that, `compose.mk` marks its namespace roots
(`io`, `flux`, `docker`, `help`, ...) `.PHONY`[^phony] automatically, so those names always run their recipe
regardless of your working directory.  Nothing to configure; dotted leaf targets like `flux.ok` are
out of scope, so avoid naming a file exactly after one.

